nss-drv: lay the wifili peer stats out for the 12.2 firmware

The 12.2 firmware writes 196-byte nss_wifili_peer_ctrl_stats entries:
its rx control block has no ucast_rcv_cnt/ucast_rcv_bytes and its retry
block has no tx_mpdu_retry_count/tx_mpdu_total_retry_count (checked
against NHSS.QSDK.12.2.r10 and 12.2.5). Built with the 12.5 layout, the
host walks the array in 212-byte steps: entry 0 is read correctly, every
later entry lands 16*i bytes off, ath11k logs "unable to find peer 0" and
throws the station statistics away - rx counters of the AP interfaces stay
at 0 and station dump never moves under Wi-Fi offload. Measured on a
GL-B3000: cm.len 200 with npeers 1 and 2, host entry 212.

Gate the four fields on NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_12_2, which the Makefile now
defines for a 12.2 build, like 0022 does for 11.4.

Signed-off-by: kuncy7 <kuncy7@openwrt-nss-edma>
--- a/exports/nss_wifili_if.h
+++ b/exports/nss_wifili_if.h
@@ -1496,9 +1496,11 @@
 	uint32_t defrag_mcast_drop;		/**< Total number of defrag multicast dropped packets. */
 #ifndef NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_11_4
 	uint32_t mcast_3addr_drop;		/**< Total number of 3 address multicast dropped packets. */
+#ifndef NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_12_2
 	uint32_t ucast_rcv_cnt;			/**< Total number of unicast packets received. */
 	uint32_t ucast_rcv_bytes;		/**< Total number of unicast bytes received. */
 #endif
+#endif
 };
 
 #ifndef NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_11_4
@@ -1511,8 +1513,10 @@
 	uint32_t tx_retry_count;		/**< Transmit retry count. */
 	uint32_t tx_multiple_retry_count;	/**< Transmit multiple retry count. */
 	uint32_t rx_retry_count;		/**< Receive retry count. */
+#ifndef NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_12_2
 	uint32_t tx_mpdu_retry_count;		/**< Per mpdu retry count. */
 	uint32_t tx_mpdu_total_retry_count;	/**< Total mpdu retry count. */
+#endif
 };
 #endif
 
